# raw tactile map clips: now TRACKED (committed for portability across machines, ~401MB).
# (previously gitignored + kept only on CRC.)
data/opentouch_states
# Same reason, for the d256 arm: extract_d256_states.py writes 166 state_*.npy plus, with
# --aux, the EMG/pose/gaze npz -- tens of MiB that are reproducible from the clips on CRC.
# Missing this rule while opentouch_states had it meant a `git add -A` on the cluster would
# have committed the whole cache.
data/d256_states
# And ActionSense's, which until 2026-08-26 was the one arm whose states WERE committed --
# 401 npy, 415 MiB. That inconsistency had a cost: deduplicating them on the cluster with
# symlinks (home is 100 GB and 68 GB used) registered as a typechange that blocked `git pull`
# twice, and each `git stash` to clear it wrote the 415 MiB straight back. Rebuild command is
# in scripts/crc/README.md; every consumer is listed there too.
data/actionsense_states
